<title>JAPAN: Yukiguni Maitake plans share buy back.</title>
<headline>Yukiguni Maitake plans share buy back.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yukiguni Maitake Co Ltd said on Thursday that it planned to spend up to 400 million yen to buy back up to 500,000 of its own shares in order to introduce a stock option scheme.</p>
<p>The company, headquartered in Niigata, central Japan, is a mushroom grower and wholesaler.</p>
<p>The company also said that one of its units would buy a 92.9 percent stake in a Tokyo-based frozen food maker.</p>
<p>Yukiguni Maitake said it expected to expand its food business through the move.</p>
</text>
